#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:6
msgid "# execute_code Multi-Runtime Design"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:8
msgid ""
"> One tool, multiple runtimes; default Node.js, extend Python / Deno on "
"demand."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:10
msgid "## Background"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:12
msgid ""
"`execute_code` was hardcoded to Node.js, but the tool schema exposed only "
"`\"Run code\"` to the LLM, causing models to frequently write Python and "
"fail execution."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:14
msgid "Goals:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:19
msgid ""
"**Clear semantics** — LLM knows which language to write and which runtime to "
"pick"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:19
msgid "**Default Bun** — same stack as FreeAnima, preferred for TS/JS snippets"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:19
msgid "**Extensible** — reserve Python, Deno, enable progressively via config"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:19
msgid "**Division from terminal** — structured subprocess vs shell"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:21
msgid "## Division from terminal"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:28
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"|           | `execute_code`                               | `terminal`                              |\n"
"| --------- | -------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n"
"| Execution | No shell, fixed runtime                      | shell=true                              |\n"
"| Best for  | Short scripts, data processing, logic checks | System commands, pipes, git, long tasks |\n"
"| Output    | 50KB cap, controllable timeout               | Same limits but more freedom            |\n"
"| Security  | Smaller attack surface (no shell injection)  | Larger attack surface                   |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:30
msgid ""
"Python batch jobs should use `execute_code(runtime=\"python\")`, not "
"`python3 -c \"...\"` in terminal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:32
msgid "## API"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:40
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"execute_code({\n"
"  code: string,           // source\n"
"  runtime?: \"bun\" | \"nodejs\" | \"python\" | \"deno\",  // default bun\n"
"  timeout?: number,       // seconds, default 300, max 600\n"
"})\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:42
msgid "### LLM-Visible Description (Principles)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:45
msgid ""
"Top-level `description` is LLM's sole source of truth (flat JSON Schema, no "
"nested wrapper)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:45
msgid ""
"State default runtime, each runtime's language, alternatives when runtime "
"disabled"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:47
msgid "## Runtime Registry"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:57
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```typescript\n"
"interface CodeRuntime {\n"
"  id: \"nodejs\" | \"python\" | \"deno\";\n"
"  enabled: boolean;\n"
"  extension: string; // .mts / .py / .ts\n"
"  preamble?: string; // bootstrap before writing file\n"
"  command: string[]; // spawn command and args (last item is file path placeholder)\n"
"}\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:64
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| runtime    | command                           | file   | preamble                      | status         |\n"
"| ---------- | --------------------------------- | ------ | ----------------------------- | -------------- |\n"
"| **bun**    | `bun` (`Bun.spawn`)               | `.ts`  | common `node:fs` imports etc. | ✅ implemented |\n"
"| **nodejs** | `node --experimental-strip-types` | `.mts` | common `node:fs` imports etc. | ✅ implemented |\n"
"| **python** | `python3`                         | `.py`  | optional `os`/`pathlib`       | 🔲 reserved    |\n"
"| **deno**   | `deno run --allow-read=...`       | `.ts`  | Deno stdlib                   | 🔲 reserved    |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:66
msgid "### Phase Plan"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:71
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Phase            | Content                                               | Status                                                          |\n"
"| ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n"
"| **P0** (current) | Flat schema + `runtime` param + bun/nodejs enabled    | ✅ implemented                                                  |\n"
"| **P1–P4**        | python / config toggles / deno / credential injection | see [#40](https://github.com/freeanima-org/freeanima/issues/40) |\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:73
msgid "## Configuration (P2 Reserved)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:87
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```yaml\n"
"execute_code:\n"
"  default_runtime: bun\n"
"  runtimes:\n"
"    nodejs:\n"
"      enabled: true\n"
"    python:\n"
"      enabled: true\n"
"      command: python3\n"
"    deno:\n"
"      enabled: false\n"
"      command: deno\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:89
msgid "Disabled runtime returns:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:93
msgid ""
"```json { \"error\": \"runtime 'python' not enabled; available: nodejs\" } "
"```"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:95
msgid "## Execution Flow"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: docs/tools/execute-code-runtimes.md:114
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"```\n"
"LLM calls execute_code(code, runtime?)\n"
"        │\n"
"        ▼\n"
"  Resolve runtime (default nodejs)\n"
"        │\n"
"        ▼\n"
"  Lookup registry → enabled?\n"
"        │ no ──→ {\"error\": \"...\"}\n"
"        ▼ yes\n"
"  mkdtemp → write preamble + code → spawn\n"
"        │\n"
"        ▼\n"
"  Merge stdout/stderr; non-zero exit → JSON { output, exit_code }\n"
"        │\n"
"        ▼\n"
"  Clean temp files\n"
"```\n"
msgstr ""

